  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID- Building Resiliency in Children (BRIC)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Iraq):  This assistance has been focusing on the prevention of radicalization and violent extremism through building children&apos;s resilience and mutual trust and tolerance of Iraq&apos;s diverse cultural and religious groups. Sesame Workshop is using early education and child development to foster individual and communal identity, to strengthen skills to counter violent extremist narratives, and to change attitudes and behaviors toward violence. Assistance will support children ages three to eight to gain foundational skills including learner readiness, social emotional learning, and appreciation for their identity and others that will allow them to accept others&apos; perspectives, resolve conflict productively, manage their own feelings, and build a sense of pride. In addition, facilitators will have increased access to high-quality professional development that will include training in strengthening children&apos;s sense of community and inclusion in the classroom, ultimately contributing to children&apos;s sense of safety, and belonging. Programming is using research, data, and learning to provide high-quality and relevant services through strategic collaboration, learning, and adaptive management.</narrative>
  </description>
